      "description": "Watch Aldosivi vs Gimnasia LP highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. Aldosivi and Gimnasia LP faced off on August 2, 2026 , in a highly anticipated Liga Profesional Argentina fixture. Both sides entered the pitch with plenty to prove, setting the stage for a contest defined by tactical discipline and moments of individual brilliance. Opening Exchanges and the First Breakthrough The match began with high physical intensity, forcing the referee to intervene early when Alan Sosa received a yellow card just 9 minutes in. Gimnasia LP had to adjust their plans prematurely as Jeremias Merlo was forced off, replaced by Agustin Colazo in the 22nd minute. Despite the disruption, the visitors maintained their composure and were rewarded shortly before half-time. In the 40th minute, Pedro Silva Torrejon delivered a precise assist for Agustin Auzmendi , who finished clinically to break the deadlock. Tactical Shifts and Doubling the Lead At the start of the second half, Aldosivi looked to alter the momentum with multiple substitutions, including the introduction of the veteran Nicolas Gaitan . However, it was Gimnasia LP who struck again. In the 66th minute, Alexis Steimbach turned provider for Agustin Colazo , who made no mistake in doubling the advantage. The game appeared to be slipping away from the hosts, but the second-half changes eventually began to pay dividends for the home side. A Grandstand Finish Hope was restored for the home fans in the 78th minute when Nicolas Gaitan found the target to pull a goal back. The strike galvanized Aldosivi , turning the final stages into a nervous battle of attrition. Gimnasia LP were forced to defend deep, picking up several cautions as Pedro Silva Torrejon and Mateo Seoane went into the book. Despite a frantic final push from the hosts during six minutes of stoppage time, the visitors held firm to secure a hard-fought victory on the road."
